From: John KNIPPER <code@jkn.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 06:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: take the stack start from the task

pthread is a static library on AROS, so v8.library carries its own copy.
That copy does not know the threads Chromium's copy created: pthread_self()
returns the main thread's id for them, and pthread_getattr_np() its stack.
cppgc then scanned the renderer thread's stack up to the main thread's stack
top, missed the roots on it, and Oilpan swept live objects: a vtable or a
member read as zero, a ScheduledAction finalised before its DOMTimer let go
(Check failed: !script_state_), in about one YouTube load in three in the
PomAROS VM. The task knows its own stack, and StackSwap keeps it current.

--- a/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc
+++ b/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc
@@ -1708,6 +1720,14 @@ bool MainThreadIsCurrentThread() {
 
 // static
 Stack::StackSlot Stack::ObtainCurrentThreadStackStart() {
+#if V8_OS_AROS
+  // pthread is a static library on AROS: this library's copy does not know
+  // the threads its embedder's copy created, and its pthread_self() names
+  // the main thread for them, so pthread_getattr_np() would return the main
+  // thread's stack and the conservative stack scan would miss every root on
+  // this one. The task knows its own stack; StackSwap keeps it current.
+  return FindTask(nullptr)->tc_SPUpper;
+#else
   pthread_attr_t attr;
   int error = pthread_getattr_np(pthread_self(), &attr);
   if (error) {
@@ -1737,6 +1757,7 @@ Stack::StackSlot Stack::ObtainCurrentThreadStackStart() {
   }
 #endif  // !defined(V8_LIBC_GLIBC)
   return stack_start;
+#endif  // V8_OS_AROS
 }
 
 #endif  // !defined(V8_OS_FREEBSD) && !defined(V8_OS_DARWIN) &&
